title: Renaissance — aggregate-on-settle closes the calibration loop (T-011)
summary: 'The highest-value governance item: the learned calibration table self-updates now. The aggregation (actuals → archetype×taskType p10/p90 bands at n≥8) was CLI-only (commands/calibrate.ts), so the moat''s learned story-points only refreshed on a manual `paradigm calibrate`. Extracted the pure logic into a shared paradigm-mcp util (calibration-aggregate.ts) so the settlement chain — which lives in MCP and couldn''t import the CLI — can call it. runSettlementChain now folds rebuildLearnedTable in as a best-effort adjacent step (not a tracked liveness stage; the probe still asserts the 3 learning stages). calibrate.ts re-exports the moved symbols (tests stay green) and uses the one shared write path. +5 tests proving the learned-graduation path end-to-end on disk. MCP 450 / CLI 441 green.'
