learnings:
  - 'The package boundary WAS the bug: aggregation in the CLI + settlement in MCP + the no-CLI-import rule = the loop physically could not close automatically. The fix is always ''extract the shared logic to the package both callers can reach'', not ''duplicate it''. Re-exporting from the original location keeps every existing import + test green during the move.'
  - Adding aggregate-on-settle as an ADJACENT best-effort step (not a tracked liveness stage) keeps the settlement-liveness probe's contract intact — the probe asserts the LEARNING chain is live; calibration refresh rides alongside without becoming something a reviewer-severed-stage test would scream about.
